:{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.5.stable\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.stable unknown - Arch Linux # 1 SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Fri, 19 Sep 2025 15:58:36 +0000 on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 2 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 Ti (nvidia; 580.82.09) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-13400F (16 threads) - 15.37 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n`LineEdit` supports Unicode code point input (`Ctrl+Shift+U` + Code Point) since 4.4. But it does not trigger `text_changed` signal.\n\nAfter further test, adding a character via the Insert Control Character options in the context menu does not trigger `text_changed` too.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nUse any `LineEdit` and check the `text_changed` signal. You can also use text boxes in the editor that reacts to empty text, e.g., the Project name input in Create Project dialog, the name input in Create Folder dialog.\n\n- Unicode code point input\n    - `Ctrl+Shift+U`, an underlined `u` appears\n    - `2020` and hit enter, an `†` character is inserted\n- Insert Control Character\n   -  Right click in the `LineEdit` and choose any option in the Insert Control Character sub menu.\n\nYou can see that `text_changed` is not emitted. (Some editor input validation output still says that it's empty.)\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/